Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: drop unconditional Samurai ready logging

The SLPI SMP2P channel carries regular traffic from other users.  The
upstream SMEM state notifier re-raises every currently asserted bit on each
incoming message, so a debug print in the ready interrupt turns ordinary
QMI traffic into an uninterruptible kernel-log storm.

The ready completion itself is unaffected.  Keep diagnostics out of the
generic remoteproc path and use tracepoints or dynamic debug instead.

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -197,10 +197,6 @@ static irqreturn_t q6v5_ready_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 {
 	struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5 = data;
 
-	if (of_machine_is_compatible("realme,samurai"))
-		dev_info(q6v5->dev, "samurai Q6 ready item=%d running=%u\n",
-			 q6v5->crash_reason, q6v5->running);
-
 	complete(&q6v5->start_done);
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
